  "description": "<p>In the HTML UI, when navigating to a binary resource that links to external content, the view should redirect to the description of the binary resource, not the binary itself.</p>\n\n<p>For example:<br/>\n&gt; curl -i -X PUT -H\"Content-Type: message/external-body; access-type=URL; URL=\\\"http://animal-dream.com/data_images/cow/cow8.jpg\\\"\" \"http://localhost:8080/rest/external\"</p>\n\n<p>In the HTML UI, navigate to the root of the repository, then click on the \"external\" link... the user should be redirected to the description instead of the external resource.</p>\n\n<p>For comparison, create a managed binary resource and navigate to it in the HTML UI:<br/>\n&gt; curl -i -X PUT -H\"Content-Type: image/png\" --data-binary @image.png \"http://localhost:8080/rest/internal\"</p>",
